# M1 / B011 — aspnet-error-handling, authentication, build-fix.

C R159 OL WF-013 | MUST | Build-fix starts from reproduction and diagnosis: reproduce the actual failure with the narrowest command, read the complete output, group errors by root cause and fix the highest-leverage cause first; for failing tests decide whether production code, setup, expectation, environment or an intentional contract change is at fault; determine the authoritative contract for cross-stack failures; update obsolete APIs from verified documentation, never fabricated. | build and test repair | none stated
C R160 OL WF-014 | MUST | Keep repair iterations small and bounded: rerun the narrowest failing verification after each meaningful fix, expand only after the focused failure is resolved, do not run unrelated build systems, stop when progress stalls and do not repeat variants of a failed guess. | build and test repair | none stated
C R161 OL WF-015 | MUST NOT | Do not weaken, delete, skip or suppress relevant tests or compiler, analyzer, TypeScript or lint failures to make verification pass (no strong-to-weak assertion swaps, no any-casts or disabled strict mode, no suppressed template diagnostics); update a test only for an intentionally requested contract change. | build and test repair | Intentionally requested contract change.
C R162 OL ARC-001,ARC-008,ARC-011,SEC-005,FE-003 | MUST NOT | A build fix must not bypass architecture to compile (Application -> Infrastructure references, persistence-technology types in Application, business logic moved into Controllers, frontend-only authorization, HTTP calls scattered into components); preserve architecture and project conventions. | build and test repair | none stated
C R163 OL WF-008 | MUST | When verification fails make the smallest appropriate fix and rerun until green or genuine user input is required; never claim the problem fixed while a known relevant failure remains; never leave the repository knowingly worse; report an unavailable toolchain instead of editing source or changing declared SDK/Node/framework versions. | verification failures | Unrelated pre-existing failures are left alone unless they block verification or the user asks.
C R164 OL WF-009 | MUST | Report verification state with PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE per area; never imply an unchecked area passed. | completion and repair reports | none stated
C R165 OL TST-010 | MUST | A behavioral test or temporary probe that establishes correct behavior is preserved per verify (Preserve Behavioral Verification) before removal; build, compiler and static-analysis commands do not require new tests. | behavioral probes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R166 OL GOV-013 | MUST NOT | Do not introduce frameworks, libraries, infrastructure or architectural patterns without a concrete current need (e.g. Identity, JWT issuance or OIDC infrastructure without an actual need). | all changes | none stated
C X19 EX DEP-010,API-010 | MUST | Register FluentValidation validators with FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions and follow the project's established validation invocation pattern rather than a second competing mechanism. | backend validation setup | none stated | DEP-010 fixes FluentValidation as the library and API-010 the validation boundaries; no oracle policy prescribes the registration package. | Registering validators through hand-written scanning deviates from the instruction.
C X20 EX WF-009 | MUST | The build-fix report states the initial failure, root cause, changes made, backend build / frontend build / tests status (PASS, NOT RUN, NOT APPLICABLE) and remaining issues. | build and test repair | none stated | WF-009 requires reporting actual verification states only; the failure/root-cause/changes sections are additional reporting duties. | A repair summary without root cause or changes made does not follow the workflow.

